Monopolistic Practices
Scope & Core Inquiries: Does this company abuse its market dominance to suppress competition, strangle innovation, or establish artificial barriers to entry? Does it engage in predatory pricing, product bundling/tying, exclusive dealing contracts, or self-preferencing on its digital or physical platforms (e.g., favoring proprietary products over third-party sellers)? Does it execute "killer acquisitions" (purchasing nascent competitors specifically to shut them down or absorb their patents)? Does it enforce closed walled gardens, aggressively restrict interoperability, block third-party repairs, or deploy patent trolling to trap consumers and businesses in its proprietary ecosystem?